                <pb facs="0932" n="812" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg812"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00 Bandit Activities, 1931/52: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Vice Consul at
                        Bluefields</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rowe</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-18T14:00:00-05:00">April 18, 1931—2
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 17, 6 p.m., third paragraph. The Naval vessels now on duty at Puerto
                    Cabezas, Bluefields, and Cape Gracias a Dios will remain until the present
                    difficulty is over.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
